item.description:
arXiv:2611.30413v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: In this paper, we investigate oscillation and non-oscillation results of second order differential equations
  \begin{equation}
  f''+(H_1e^z+H_2e^{\alpha z}+q)f=0,\tag{+}
  \end{equation} where $H_1,H_2\in\C\setminus\{0\}$, $0<\alpha<1$, and $q$ is an entire function of order less than $1$. First, we show that if equation (+) has a zero-free non-trivial entire solution, then either $\alpha=1/2$ or $\alpha=3/4$, which settles the Problem 9 posed in \cite{HITW}. Second, we prove that if either $q$ is transcendental, or $\alpha=(2m-1)/(2m)$ for some integer $m\geq 2$ and $q\equiv 0$, then every non-trivial entire solution $f$ of $(+)$ satisfies $\lambda(f)=\infty$.
